<h1>About</h1>
<figure class="float-right" style="max-width: 36%;">
    <img src="/assets/me.jpeg" alt="Me at Memorial Terrace in graduation regalia.">
</figure>
<p>
    I'm Nico, a software engineer from Wisconsin! My interests in tech span full-stack development, performance engineering, and parallelism—and, especially, how we can apply traditional performance principles to AI systems.
    In my free time, I <a href="/writing">write</a> about computing, history, and philosophy.
    I also like to draw, <a href="https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/155270767-nico" target="_blank">read (paper) books</a>, and recently started to get into climbing.

<p>
You can find me on <a href="https://github.com/nicosalm" target="_blank">GitHub</a>, <a href="https://x.com/salmdotdev" target="_blank">Twitter</a>, or say hi via <a href="#" data-email="ved.mlas@ocin">email [<span class="copy-label">copy</span>]</a>!
</p>

</p>

<h2>Now</h2>
<p>
    Right now, I build all sorts of AI and ML tools for the clinical teams I support in my role as a software engineer in "big pharma"—
    I'm also learning more about performance on the side, with a pinch or two of theory.
</p>
<p>
I post monthly updates to my <a href="/now">now page</a>.
</p>
<h2>Studies</h2>
<p>
    In 2026, I graduated from the <a href="/writing/my-wisconsin-experience/">University of Wisconsin-Madison</a> with a B.S. in Computer Sciences and Data Science. I spent most of my time hanging out in the
    <a href="https://www.upl.cs.wisc.edu/" target="_blank">UPL</a> on campus with my <a href="/misc#friends">friends</a>.
</p>
<p>
    For two years, I was a member of the <a href="https://skunkworks.engr.wisc.edu/" target="_blank">Informatics Skunkworks</a> research group, led by Dr. Dane Morgan, where I trained generative models to design new crystal structures with target physical properties. I helped found the <a href="https://wqi.wisc.edu/wqcc/" target="_blank">Wisconsin Quantum Computing Club</a> as one of its first four officers, and later competed with the group at <a href="https://www.iquise.mit.edu/iQuHACK/2024-02-02" target="_blank">MIT's IQuHACK</a>. At the UPL, I served as a lab coordinator, introduced its <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@undergraduateprojectslab" target="_blank">Lightning Talks</a>, and helped organize <a href="https://www.madhacks.io/" target="_blank">MadHacks</a>, growing it to a record 417 participants.
</p>

<h2>Colophon</h2>
<p>
    This site is built with <a href="https://www.11ty.dev/" target="_blank">Eleventy</a>, HTML, and CSS. No JavaScript by default; posts that need it pull in MathJax, a table of contents, sidenotes, or category filters. Images are converted to AVIF at build time, and links prefetch on hover via <a href="https://instant.page/" target="_blank">instant.page</a>. There's an <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a> and a <a href="/sitemap.xml">sitemap</a>.
</p>
<p>Source <a href="https://github.com/nicosalm/salm.dev/" target="_blank">on GitHub</a>.</p>

